<title>UK: Banco BMC sets $50 mln step-up eight-year bond.</title>
<headline>Banco BMC sets $50 mln step-up eight-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager WestMerchant.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANCO BMC</p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 COUPON    *10.25     MATURITY  **22.MAY.05</p>
<p> TYPE	 STEP-UP   ISS PRICE  99.8233   PAY DATE    12.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.875     REOFFER    99.8233   SPREAD	+395 BP</p>
<p> REOFF YD   10.32     LISTING    =LUX	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS UK/BZ</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC   0.375</p>
<p> NOTES	*TO THE FIRST PUT AND CALL, WITH A STEP UP TO 10.50</p>
<p>PCT IN YEAR THREE TO YEAR FIVE THEN STEPS UP TO 10.75 PCT UNTIL MATURITY.</p>
<p>	     **CALLS AND PUTS AT PAR ON 22.MAY.00 AND 22.MAY.02 --</p>
<p>London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
